    "temperature": {
      "file": "grease_lubrication_system_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Right amount, right interval",
      "description": "Grease = base oil held in a thickener; the bearing takes oil from it. Too little starves the bearing; too much churns and overheats it (temperature rises for hours after over-greasing). Relubricate with a quantity G ≈ 0.005 × D × B (grams; D = OD, B = width in mm) at intervals from the maker's charts (speed factor n·dm, temperature, contamination), with the relief plug open so old grease can escape. Never mix incompatible thickeners.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
